WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.040
These three students in Sweden almost got banned from their university for creating an AI learning system.

00:05.160 --> 00:10.740
The first month we launched, we reached 130,000 euro ARR.

00:10.880 --> 00:12.640
It was like pure word of mouth growth.

00:12.940 --> 00:17.520
They actually called us in and wanted us to stop what we were doing.

00:17.760 --> 00:21.560
This is Isabel, Andreas and Eric, and in the last six months, they dropped out of college,

00:21.820 --> 00:25.020
moved into a 25 square meter apartment, and snuck into a Google event,

00:25.120 --> 00:27.560
all on a mission to reinvent how people learn.

00:27.560 --> 00:32.300
Is the best way to learn stuff by reading a book or going to lectures and such?

00:32.500 --> 00:33.700
I don't think so, personally.

00:33.920 --> 00:38.320
The year is 1088 and Bologna opens the first university for the smartest people across the

00:38.320 --> 00:38.560
world.

00:38.800 --> 00:41.380
A thousand years later, the system hasn't changed.

00:41.640 --> 00:45.760
Because while universities cost more than ever, 40% of students will drop out before

00:45.760 --> 00:46.920
they finish their degree.

00:47.200 --> 00:48.000
I have ADHD.

00:48.560 --> 00:49.940
I managed school.

00:50.380 --> 00:53.660
I did get the good grades, but it was very tough.

00:54.020 --> 00:55.500
Everyone learns differently.

00:55.500 --> 01:02.540
It's a system that needs to be personalized and adapt for every human that learns in different ways.

01:02.860 --> 01:08.640
So instead of forcing students to learn the old-fashioned way, they left their lives behind and bet everything on Klar.

01:08.900 --> 01:12.620
Basically, it's your private teacher in your phone or your laptop or whatever.

01:12.800 --> 01:20.720
If you need flashcards, if you need a video, if you need an image, if you need an explainer, a summary, a test to quiz yourself on, it can do that.

01:20.980 --> 01:22.260
And it always knows where you're at.

01:22.260 --> 01:24.720
Thousands of students were waiting to learn differently.

01:25.040 --> 01:27.820
It was time to turn Klar from an idea into reality.

01:28.140 --> 01:32.940
I've always had these big visions and big ideas that I wanted to create.

01:33.220 --> 01:39.520
When Lovable came and I first tried it out, it completely changed everything for me.

01:39.680 --> 01:46.300
We now have a partnership with a company that's owning all the economic facilities in Sweden.

01:46.600 --> 01:49.280
That's 35,000 students.

01:49.280 --> 01:57.140
And now we're gonna be around all of Sweden, we have some things going on in the US and also Europe, Spain, Madrid.

01:57.360 --> 02:04.500
We obviously have like students or friends that reach out to us and said like, hey, thank you so much.

02:04.580 --> 02:08.460
I had such a bad teacher and I still passed because of you guys.

02:08.620 --> 02:10.240
And I was like, okay, that feels good.

02:10.360 --> 02:14.180
And now the same university that tried to stop them is asking to work with them.

02:14.360 --> 02:18.840
Because after a thousand years of education, all it took was three friends to change it.
